# L §2.5: "A key literal that could belong to two indexes, kinds or axes in one position is refused (LOAD-KEY)."
# k == b: b is a key of both ks and js, and k ranges over a key list whose index no key position fixes.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

index ks = [a, b]
index js = [b, c]

def n: int = count(k in [a, b] where k == b)

ask q1: n
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY ...
